{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01QX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$i_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:13cce919ba782f124f971e6edff8163915e6d4553ad6ddabda93ee3b4804e3eb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d40ef2a86ae5cfcb3bf62a19d613bf86ec0e31656055e5b333bb3c224c9ff532", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a closed immersion. Because of the lemma above we often,\nby abuse of notation, denote <MATH_0002> the sheaf <MATH_0003> on <MATH_0004>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4d5d8be2e5ab00f005880e75e46e2e8313f9360acb06cb60ca3f54c13c82c28e", "unit_id": "tag:01QX:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01QX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G} \\subset \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{G}' \\subset \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{H}$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_X}(\\mathcal{H}, \\mathcal{G}')\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_X}(\\mathcal{H}, \\mathcal{G})\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{G}'$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{G}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-largest-quasi-coherent-subsheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0d5b440cc21c376e31a76073e89cbb31db88fd04004cd8bb5bb6ac3394e04b97", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9e9409bb8adc2fc71f44c498c1de43380fe080cc788e9337de36c92256e23a15", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0003>-module. Let <MATH_0004>\nbe a <MATH_0005>-submodule. There exists a unique quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0006>-submodule <MATH_0007>\nwith the following property: For every quasi-coherent <MATH_0008>-module\n<MATH_0009> the map\n<MATH_0010>\nis bijective. In particular <MATH_0011> is the largest quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0012>-submodule of <MATH_0013> contained in <MATH_0014>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9fd7292e5bdac04883e4cf86d07adc42f820dd39f0054e1e402c25101b814384", "unit_id": "tag:01QZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01QX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{G}_a$", "MATH_0002": "$a \\in A$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{G}'$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{a \\in A} \\mathcal{G}_a \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{F}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{G}'$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{H}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0014": "$\\alpha : \\mathcal{H} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{H} \\to \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{G}'$", "MATH_0018": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{G}'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-section-quasi-coherent}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:421391d410c2b07648098183a1e6c4e82a643076d0fc0becb141d53684e7f02c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:39a8153b9884918e85d312e874725172dd015866767b628f70b2dc19b972d442", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be the set of quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0003>-submodules contained in <MATH_0004>.\nThen the image <MATH_0005> of\n<MATH_0006>\nis quasi-coherent as the image of a map of quasi-coherent sheaves\non <MATH_0007> is quasi-coherent and since a direct sum of quasi-coherent sheaves\nis quasi-coherent, see\nSchemes, Section <REF_0001>.\nThe module <MATH_0008> is contained in <MATH_0009>. Hence this is the\nlargest quasi-coherent <MATH_0010>-module contained in <MATH_0011>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nTo prove the formula, let <MATH_0012> be a quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0013>-module and let <MATH_0014>\nbe an <MATH_0015>-module map. The image of the composition\n<MATH_0016> is quasi-coherent\nas the image of a map of quasi-coherent sheaves. Hence it is contained\nin <MATH_0017>. Hence <MATH_0018> factors through <MATH_0019>\nas desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f194b3e6f26c09ac16716c1dbbd7306e8bf2deb8104ae53c36a06663835210ca", "unit_id": "tag:01QZ:proof"}
